WEBVTT

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.830
Sturm Beta seems to be functioning well.

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.540
Of course.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.560
It's natural for a new model to be more powerful than an old one.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.840
But...

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.340
Argevollen is still stronger.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.070
Disturbance
Disturbance

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:00.340
I heard the 5th division got wiped out at Rodamisaki.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.320
Supposedly.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.470
A guy I once knew was there.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.580
I wonder if he's okay.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.860
I heard they pulled back 20 kilometers to reorganize.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.110
Why not ask?

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:10.960
I guess.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.990
Yeah.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:13.880
Oh, stop.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.960
I'm just kidding.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.160
Oh, they're here.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.950
Hey.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.330
Don't touch it, dummy!

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:34.270
Welcome back.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.410
That looked like it hurt.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.780
Bye, you two.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.780
Idle hands are the devil's workshop.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.500
Sergeant Major...

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.290
How long have you been there?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.540
Idle hands are the what, now?

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.740
Look it up.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.830
Chief, here's the #32 fluid coupler.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.500
Okay, give it here.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:37.900
We ran a diagnostic on the Seiran 2's hydraulic circuits three days ago.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.090
That was three whole days ago.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.730
This thing's dampers have to bear a lot more weight than Argevollen.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.970
If there are any parts we can swap out, we should do it while we can.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.800
Hikaru.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.310
Open up the upper receiver later and measure the field ramp alignment.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:53.980
Okay!

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:59.920
So, what if the enemy comes up through the northern hills, like this?

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.370
We lay down fire.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.240
We can shoot through side armor.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.920
I see.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:08.530
So we let Tokimune-kun handle the front.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.120
And what will you do, Lorenz-san?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.520
The Seiran 2 will stand by on the southern plateau along with Namie-chan as backup.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.550
Man, that's not fair.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.590
What do you mean, "it's not fair"?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.460
Fight with me!

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.830
No complaining.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.520
You're better suited for this.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.800
Tokimune-senpai will be okay, right?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.050
Yeah.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.100
Take care of him.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.140
Oh, here's my backup!

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.320
What does that mean?

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.110
Just ignore him.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.500
Noise?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.380
Yes.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.120
The only plausible reason that Argevollen's pilot is still alive

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.310
is the noise in the U-Link.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.870
Then we must be grateful to that pilot.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:03.380
It's fair to say that our technology has dramatically advanced as a result of this.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:09.390
It's impossible to say how much this will affect Trail Krieger development in the future.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.030
That's right.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:14.020
Tell His Excellency Cayenne I said hello.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.410
And that we'll give whatever help he needs.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.820
Ingelmia's addition of Sturm Beta

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.250
allowed them to gain the upper hand once more

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.910
in what had been a stabilizing situation.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.650
The Great Wall, which had once been a fortress that protected Arandas,

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.720
was taken over by Ingelmia

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.530
and transformed into their most important base in the war.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:45.960
Meanwhile, Arandas was forced to draw back its troops,

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.010
and fight the invasion by bringing its troops closer together.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:54.870
But anyone could see that a battle of retreat fought with no outside aid

00:06:54.870 --> 00:07:00.940
was nothing but a prolonged suicide on the nation's part.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.770
From this information,

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.450
we can assume that the large-scale force gathered at the Great Wall

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:12.660
will be used for a final attack on Ajuas.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.250
There are still things we can do.

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:29.190
I still intend to attempt my counterattack with my Perpevollen forces.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.680
My forces will gather at a single point,

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.410
and advance into the hills of Zianxec.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:43.270
This is where the enemy forces are thinnest,

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.980
and by crossing the Silabisk River here from the north,

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:50.410
we can cut Ingelmia's supply lines and leave out their rear—

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.030
Brigadier General Cayenne.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.410
Cancel that order.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.660
I believe some of you have heard this,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.920
but the High Privy Council has settled on making peace with Ingelmia.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.660
Any further battles will simply exhaust the country for nothing,

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.900
and make it harder to recover.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:18.810
We must build a future for Arandas.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.680
A future?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.430
What about the future

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:30.070
of the soldiers who are covered in blood and crawling through gun smoke this very minute?

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.120
We are soldiers.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.100
Soldiers obey orders!

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:35.070
Cayenne!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.070
That's enough.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:41.830
Those soldiers offered up their lives to protect the future of their countrymen.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:45.830
I'm sure you're trying to settle this with platitudes, but that won't happen.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:51.970
You're just repeating the words of the Privy Council because all you care about is yourselves!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.090
Cayenne! Watch your mouth!

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:56.590
The decision has already been made.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.350
Maybe you should watch <i>your</i> mouth!

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:06.500
I've put up with your nonsense because I believed

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.110
that Arandas's future lay beyond this battle.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.000
But I'm done with that.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.110
What are you saying?

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.880
I'm saying I've had it with you.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.120
What do you think you're doing?

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:26.790
Where are you going?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:28.630
The conference isn't over!

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.880
You can sit there and warm your chairs until you die.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:35.970
From now on, I'll do what I want.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.800
Are you sure about this?

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.660
If you come with me, you won't be able to stay in the military.

00:10:04.030 --> 00:10:06.530
I believe in you, Brigadier General Cayenne, and I'll follow you!

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:07.410
Me, too!

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.920
All we have is victory!

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.920
Give us your orders, sir!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.460
All those who agree with us

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.180
are waiting for you to give the order!

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:19.680
All right.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.970
I, Toshikazu Cayenne,

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.870
will take responsibility for your lives.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:28.150
Brigadier General Cayenne, removed from duty?

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:30.350
He probably will be soon enough.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.880
But this was more like a rebellion than being removed.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:36.610
He left on his own.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:41.120
Does that mean Captain Samonji will be caught up in that?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.250
It does.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.120
But I don't think you need to worry.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.060
Colonel, are you planning to do something with Captain Samonji?

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.140
What do you mean, "something"?

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.130
Well...

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.410
It's true that he and I have known each other for a long time.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:03.140
But nobody knows what he's thinking.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:08.030
Once Samonji decides to do something, he does it.

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:09.890
He won't let anyone stop him.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:14.110
And he left your unit without saying anything.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:17.900
That means he doesn't want you all getting involved anymore.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.400
I can't accept that.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.200
He doesn't care whether you accept it or not.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:27.020
That's the kind of man he is.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:41.940
We'll be going to Zianxec as planned.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.820
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.290
I'll make my base here.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.770
Go kick some butt.

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:54.020
You and I are in charge of this war now.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:06.660
My beloved soldiers,

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.920
the time when we release the people of Arandas

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.870
from their suffering under the corrupt oppression of their monarchy is nigh.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.130
Load your guns!

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.880
Sharpen your blades!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.240
Justice is with you!

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:19.640
Hurrah for Ingelmia!

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.380
Sorry to keep you waiting.
Hurrah for Ingelmia!

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:24.750
Hurrah for our great leader Junios!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:24.780
Hurrah for our leader.
Hurrah for our great leader Junios!

00:12:24.780 --> 00:12:25.250
Hurrah for our leader.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:26.530
Hurrah for Ingelmia!
Hurrah for our leader.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.330
Hurrah for Ingelmia!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:27.890
Hurr–

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:34.140
We got this information from an Arandain traitor two days ago.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.620
The Type-16.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.120
Also known as Perfevollen.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.100
It's a mass-produced Argevollen.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:45.200
Its capabilities exceed those of Sturm Beta.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:49.450
But we have far more machines in the field.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:53.460
It's impossible to turn the tide of the war with a single new model.

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:57.820
You noticed, huh?

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:01.040
Yes. This machine is very unique.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.350
You could almost call it original.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:06.150
Yes.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.970
This Trail Krieger is unmanned.

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:12.870
I'm sure there's no need to explain how much of a threat a Trail Krieger

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:18.360
that doesn't need to account for the physical limits of the pilot can be.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:24.090
We must be prepared for the possibility that a single unit could affect the outcome of the war.

00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:29.130
And this is the best part of the information we got.

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:32.060
Is this Arandas's unit operation plan?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:32.940
Yes.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.160
For the Perfevollen unit.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.390
This is their most elite special forces unit.

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:41.410
Where it will go, and what routes it will take,

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.920
are top secret classified information.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:45.920
Who is this man?

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.340
Ukyo Samonji.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.070
The commander of the Perfevollen unit.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:55.930
It seems he's using the U-Link to control all the Perfevollens.

00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.310
All alone?

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.470
We don't know the technological details.

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:05.290
But from the data we have, that appears to be the case.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.320
I'm amazed you got this.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:12.010
You said it's from an Arandain traitor?

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.580
They're fighting over any number of things on their side, it seems.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:21.420
Let's just say it's from a group that doesn't appreciate the Perfevollens.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.960
You spent a lot of effort preparing this, Lontar.

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:27.850
Thank you. I'm honored.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.710
Okay! Next!

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:09.230
Direction 02. Distance 3000.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:10.220
Enemy combat vehicle.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:11.550
Roger!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.540
Time to blow them away!

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.600
Get <i>back!</i>

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.050
Tokimune!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.470
Behind you!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.190
That was...

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:10.560
Jamie-san...

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:25.210
No enemy activity in the vicinity.

00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.980
Mission complete.

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:29.560
Tell them to move to alert level 3.

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:30.090
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.350
Attention all units.

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:33.830
Mission complete.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.090
Move to alert level 3.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.340
I repeat. Mission complete.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.720
Move to alert level 3.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:56.850
Jamie...

00:16:56.850 --> 00:16:58.080
Are you okay?

00:16:58.550 --> 00:16:59.740
Yeah.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.680
Back there...

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.760
I heard your voice.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.340
Yeah.

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.000
I see.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:23.520
A transfer order?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.920
That's right.

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.760
Colonel Shizuma Izumi,

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:31.520
you are to be transferred to the direct control of the High Privy Council.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.740
The High Privy Council?

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.530
Then...

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.480
I see you understand.

00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:45.040
You're going to lead the team pushing for the peace process with Ingelmia.

00:17:45.490 --> 00:17:49.240
I don't know if a young person like myself can do that...

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.920
Don't be so modest.

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.160
When the war is over,

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:57.300
Arandas will need smart and young officers like you.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.450
Yes, I'm honored.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.790
If you would permit me to,

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.190
I'd like to report this to Brigadier General Cayenne...

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.690
A order has been issued for Toshikazu Cayenne's arrest.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:13.770
An arrest order?

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:15.440
For what?

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.000
His repeated failure to execute orders.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.790
We have a very high opinion of you.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:30.230
I'm sure you know exactly who you should side with.

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:34.920
Yes, sir.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:36.970
I'm grateful for your kindness.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.610
So the old men have finally gotten off their butts, huh?

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:52.360
Looks like they've sent MPs to arrest me.

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.190
But it's too late.

00:19:02.860 --> 00:19:04.370
How are the preparations going?

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.820
Our comrades are on standby in Gazaka's second army

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.440
and Idogaya's Royal Guard Regiment!

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:12.630
Lt. Colonel Shishikura is mobilizing the reserves under his command!

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:17.030
All our comrades are awaiting your orders!

00:19:17.030 --> 00:19:17.880
I see!

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:24.430
I'll show those old men who it is that makes history.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.270
Attention all soldiers!

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.760
I am the commander of the Arandas Northwest theater forces,

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.480
Toshikazu Cayenne.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:42.990
Today, I have an important announcement for you.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:50.000
Did you know that the villains at the heart of the Arandas defense forces

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.200
are preparing to commit a cowardly act of betrayal against you?

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.000
You have sacrificed your bodies

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:02.680
and risked your lives to protect the land and families you love.

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:07.630
This is because you had a firm belief

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:10.180
that victory was the only thing that could protect Arandas.

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:15.050
But the military brass has come to the despicable decision to surrender,

00:20:15.050 --> 00:20:20.190
based on the present state of the war.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:22.440
Do not be deceived.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:24.700
This is a false peace!

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:29.710
Those who seek peace with Ingelmia seek only their own protection,

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.880
and to monopolize the wealth that will come after the war's end.

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:38.960
A true noble spirit that seeks peace does not exist in them!

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.210
Stand, soldiers!

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:45.470
The core of the military is not the corrupt generals!

00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.840
What is this transmission?

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.530
Where is it coming from?

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:50.720
We don't know.

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:55.000
It's using a top-priority code to force its way onto all channels!

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.230
Curse you, Cayenne.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.360
What's going on?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.670
Reporting!

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:06.640
Some of the soldiers have answered Brigadier General Cayenne's call and taken up arms!

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:07.620
What?!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:14.500
We will win this war!

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:17.630
You must not stop your advance!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:25.680
This is the beginning.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:30.010
Victory is the only thing we want!

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:35.020
I swear Arandas will be victorious!

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:40.020
I vow to praise the glory of the heroic spirits who have fallen on the battlefield forever!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.530
Rise, soldiers!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.130
Wipe away the villains of a ruined country,

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:48.340
and lead Arandas to victory with me!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:13.430
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:19.650
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:26.280
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:32.950
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:40.750
I remember that I can't

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:47.380
rationalize everything

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:54.560
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:55.810 --> 00:23:02.560
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:02.560 --> 00:23:08.700
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:16.080
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:22.670
It'll reach you someday.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:39.570
Capture
